name: sim.intersectPointsWithPointCloud
description: Removes points from a point cloud, that do not intersect with the provided points (i.e. the result in the point cloud will be the intersection between the two sets of points). When a point cloud doesn't use an OC tree calculation structure, then this operation cannot be performed
luaSynopsis: int totalPointCnt = sim.intersectPointsWithPointCloud(int pcHandle, int options, list points, float tolerance)
pythonSynopsis: int totalPointCnt = sim.intersectPointsWithPointCloud(int pcHandle, int options, float[] points, float tolerance)
inputs:
1. pcHandle: handle of the point cloud
2. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 set (1): specified points are relative to the point cloud reference frame, otherwise they are relative to the world reference frame
3. points: array of point positions specified as x/y/z coordinates
4. tolerance: distance used as a tolerance value
outputs:
1. totalPointCnt: the total number of points in the point cloud
replacedBy:
- name: intersectPoints, class: pointCloud, file: pointCloud_intersectPoints.method
- name: intersectPackedPoints, class: pointCloud, file: pointCloud_intersectPackedPoints.method
